Subject: Resolves #170 Tests failing on Ubuntu Noble, giftext buffer overflow

giftext formats each printable byte of the text dump into a one-character slot of AsciiForm with snprintf(&AsciiForm[CrntPlace], 3, "%c", ...). At CrntPlace == 15 only two bytes remain, so the declared size of 3 exceeds the space left, and FORTIFY_SOURCE aborts the giftext regression. The write is always one character plus a NUL, so the output is unchanged; the size argument becomes 2.

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/sailfishos-mirror/giflib/commit/c5e0a61f56022eb2315e211ede9ccd36c6779d88
Base-Tree: debian giflib 5.2.2-1+deb13u1
Description: Upstream giflib project is at SourceForge (git.code.sf.net/p/giflib/code); the commit is the same SHA as in the GitHub mirror.
Verify: cmd `make -C tests` expect "No output is good news"

--- a/giftext.c
+++ b/giftext.c
@@ -442,7 +442,7 @@
 		for (i = 1; i <= Len; i++) {
 			(void)snprintf(&HexForm[CrntPlace * 3], 3, " %02x",
 			               Extension[i]);
-			(void)snprintf(&AsciiForm[CrntPlace], 3, "%c",
+			(void)snprintf(&AsciiForm[CrntPlace], 2, "%c",
 			               MAKE_PRINTABLE(Extension[i]));
 			if (++CrntPlace == 16) {
 				HexForm[CrntPlace * 3] = 0;
@@ -488,7 +488,7 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < Len; i++) {
 		(void)snprintf(&HexForm[CrntPlace * 3], 3, " %02x",
 		               PixelBlock[i]);
-		(void)snprintf(&AsciiForm[CrntPlace], 3, "%c",
+		(void)snprintf(&AsciiForm[CrntPlace], 2, "%c",
 		               MAKE_PRINTABLE(PixelBlock[i]));
 		if (++CrntPlace == 16) {
 			HexForm[CrntPlace * 3] = 0;
